{
  "0": [
    {
      "text": "Why does the silver eagle look",
      "startSec": 0.08,
      "endSec": 1.82
    },
    {
      "text": "different even though it carries the",
      "startSec": 1.82,
      "endSec": 3.38
    },
    {
      "text": "familiar eagle design?",
      "startSec": 3.38,
      "endSec": 4.42
    }
  ],
  "1": [
    {
      "text": "The answer is in the finish.",
      "startSec": 0.05,
      "endSec": 1.63
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a 2021 West Point Type",
      "startSec": 7.97,
      "endSec": 9.83
    },
    {
      "text": "1 reverse proof, and its label",
      "startSec": 9.83,
      "endSec": 11.89
    },
    {
      "text": "tells several different stories that are",
      "startSec": 11.89,
      "endSec": 13.61
    },
    {
      "text": "easy to mix together.",
      "startSec": 13.61,
      "endSec": 14.47
    }
  ],
  "2": [
    {
      "text": "Start with the surface.",
      "startSec": 0.05,
      "endSec": 1.19
    },
    {
      "text": "On a conventional proof, the background",
      "startSec": 2.25,
      "endSec": 3.85
    },
    {
      "text": "is reflective and the raised design",
      "startSec": 3.85,
      "endSec": 5.83
    },
    {
      "text": "is frosted.",
      "startSec": 5.83,
      "endSec": 6.51
    },
    {
      "text": "A reverse proof switches the contrast,",
      "startSec": 6.89,
      "endSec": 8.61
    },
    {
      "text": "the background is frosted, while the",
      "startSec": 9.07,
      "endSec": 10.69
    },
    {
      "text": "design has a mirrorlike finish.",
      "startSec": 10.69,
      "endSec": 12.11
    }
  ],
  "3": [
    {
      "text": "That means reverse proof describes how",
      "startSec": 0.05,
      "endSec": 2.37
    },
    {
      "text": "the coin looks.",
      "startSec": 2.37,
      "endSec": 3.15
    },
    {
      "text": "It does not mean the eagle",
      "startSec": 3.87,
      "endSec": 4.95
    },
    {
      "text": "is facing backward, or that only",
      "startSec": 4.95,
      "endSec": 7.01
    },
    {
      "text": "the back received a special finish.",
      "startSec": 7.01,
      "endSec": 8.59
    }
  ],
  "4": [
    {
      "text": "Now, look at the eagle and",
      "startSec": 0.08,
      "endSec": 1.62
    },
    {
      "text": "shield.",
      "startSec": 1.62,
      "endSec": 1.82
    },
    {
      "text": "This is John Mercanti's heraldic eagle,",
      "startSec": 3.02,
      "endSec": 5.12
    },
    {
      "text": "the reverse design introduced with the",
      "startSec": 5.8,
      "endSec": 7.68
    },
    {
      "text": "Silver Eagle in 1986.",
      "startSec": 7.68,
      "endSec": 9.34
    },
    {
      "text": "The W below the design identifies",
      "startSec": 10.04,
      "endSec": 12.44
    },
    {
      "text": "West Point.",
      "startSec": 12.44,
      "endSec": 13.4
    }
  ],
  "5": [
    {
      "text": "In 2021, the American Eagle program",
      "startSec": 0.02,
      "endSec": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "reached its 35th anniversary.",
      "startSec": 3,
      "endSec": 4.54
    },
    {
      "text": "The mint marked that transition with",
      "startSec": 5.72,
      "endSec": 7.36
    },
    {
      "text": "a designer edition set pairing two",
      "startSec": 7.36,
      "endSec": 9.26
    },
    {
      "text": "reverse proofs.",
      "startSec": 9.26,
      "endSec": 9.9
    },
    {
      "text": "The original design from West Point",
      "startSec": 10.78,
      "endSec": 12.34
    },
    {
      "text": "and the new design from San",
      "startSec": 12.34,
      "endSec": 14.06
    },
    {
      "text": "Francisco.",
      "startSec": 14.06,
      "endSec": 14.56
    }
  ],
  "6": [
    {
      "text": "Sales opened September 13th.",
      "startSec": 0.05,
      "endSec": 2.27
    },
    {
      "text": "The announced production limit was",
      "startSec": 2.83,
      "endSec": 4.61
    },
    {
      "text": "125,000 sets.",
      "startSec": 4.61,
      "endSec": 5.77
    },
    {
      "text": "That was a set limit, not",
      "startSec": 6.59,
      "endSec": 7.73
    },
    {
      "text": "a count of coins graded 70.",
      "startSec": 7.73,
      "endSec": 9.23
    }
  ],
  "7": [
    {
      "text": "The holder here reads reverse PF70,",
      "startSec": 0.05,
      "endSec": 2.65
    },
    {
      "text": "NGC defines a 70 as having",
      "startSec": 3.39,
      "endSec": 5.29
    },
    {
      "text": "no post-production imperfections visible at",
      "startSec": 5.29,
      "endSec": 7.73
    },
    {
      "text": "5 times magnification.",
      "startSec": 7.73,
      "endSec": 8.87
    },
    {
      "text": "That grade describes condition under its",
      "startSec": 10.15,
      "endSec": 12.11
    },
    {
      "text": "standard, while Type 1 identifies the",
      "startSec": 12.11,
      "endSec": 14.51
    },
    {
      "text": "design.",
      "startSec": 14.51,
      "endSec": 14.75
    }
  ],
  "8": [
    {
      "text": "First day of issue is another",
      "startSec": 0.08,
      "endSec": 1.68
    },
    {
      "text": "distinction.",
      "startSec": 1.68,
      "endSec": 2.32
    },
    {
      "text": "NGC's published requirements tied it to",
      "startSec": 2.96,
      "endSec": 5.2
    },
    {
      "text": "purchase and receipt deadlines supported by",
      "startSec": 5.2,
      "endSec": 7.82
    },
    {
      "text": "evidence.",
      "startSec": 7.82,
      "endSec": 8.12
    },
    {
      "text": "It does not establish the day",
      "startSec": 8.8,
      "endSec": 10.34
    },
    {
      "text": "this individual coin was struck.",
      "startSec": 10.34,
      "endSec": 12.04
    }
  ],
  "9": [
    {
      "text": "So, this label separates design, finish,",
      "startSec": 0.02,
      "endSec": 3.12
    },
    {
      "text": "condition, and release designation.",
      "startSec": 3.66,
      "endSec": 5.24
    },
    {
      "text": "For me, the appeal starts with",
      "startSec": 7.4,
      "endSec": 9.24
    },
    {
      "text": "seeing that familiar, heraldic eagle against",
      "startSec": 9.24,
      "endSec": 11.62
    },
    {
      "text": "a completely different surface.",
      "startSec": 11.62,
      "endSec": 13.04
    }
  ],
  "10": [
    {
      "text": "Which catches your eye first the",
      "startSec": 0.02,
      "endSec": 2.36
    },
    {
      "text": "finish or the eagle?",
      "startSec": 2.36,
      "endSec": 3.48
    }
  ]
}
